# Decisions

> The anti-drift anchor for commitments that span multiple rounds and are not
> owned by any single round doc.

A decision here is a promise: *"we agreed not to build X until Y"*, *"we chose
A over B and will not revisit before Z"*. Round docs record what happened in
one round; this records what holds across all of them.

## What goes here

- A commitment that outlives the round that made it
- A deliberate non-goal, and the condition that would reopen it
- A choice between two viable designs, with the losing option and why

## What does not

| Instead of here | Put it in | Because |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A finding or observation | `memory/` | It is evidence, not a commitment |
| What happened this round | `plan/cycles/Round_NNN.md` | Round-scoped by definition |
| A promotion into canon | `plan/promotions.md` | That log has its own format |
| A rule agents must follow | `context/` | Canon is loaded; this is not |

## Format

Copy [`_TEMPLATE.md`](_TEMPLATE.md). One decision per file, named
`YYYY-MM-DD-short-topic.md`.

Decisions are **append-only**. Superseding one does not delete it: set its
status and link forward, so the reason the old choice was made survives.
